  "summary_en": "Danish executive order setting rules for trials of self-driving motor vehicles up to SAE level 4. The Road Directorate issues permits of up to two years, requires a licensed human driver or operator able to take over, data logging, a safety assessment by an approved assessor, and penalties. It repeals four earlier local trial orders.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Trials allowed up to SAE J3016 level 4 in defined areas and times",
   "Vejdirektoratet grants permits for up to 2 years, renewable and revocable at any time",
   "A licensed physical driver or operator must be able to take over control",
   "Applicants must submit a data plan and an approved assessor's road-safety impact assessment",
   "Permit holders and legal persons face fines and criminal liability; four earlier trial orders are repealed"
